WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.164 --> 00:00:03.072
(siren)
- I could smell the smoke,

00:00:03.072 --> 00:00:07.829
and I could see the flames
shooting way up in the sky.

00:00:07.829 --> 00:00:09.451
You think, "Is this real?"

00:00:09.451 --> 00:00:11.284
It was like a nightmare.

00:00:11.284 --> 00:00:12.692
(crashing)

00:00:12.692 --> 00:00:15.019
My kids were there, my wife was there,

00:00:15.019 --> 00:00:17.186
inside a few hours before.

00:00:19.682 --> 00:00:23.388
To think that somebody
not only burned the mosque

00:00:23.388 --> 00:00:26.319
but is trying to burn
everything that you believed in,

00:00:26.319 --> 00:00:29.969
that no, you're not part
of this American fabric.

00:00:29.969 --> 00:00:32.595
(sorrowful strings)

00:00:32.595 --> 00:00:35.052
I kept thinking, "What is going on here?"

00:00:35.052 --> 00:00:38.520
You know, we live here,
our kids grew up here.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:39.683
Are we wanted?

00:00:39.683 --> 00:00:40.899
Are we welcome?

00:00:40.899 --> 00:00:44.469
Is this a goodbye eviction notice?

00:00:44.469 --> 00:00:47.469
(soft piano melody)

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:56.856
- When I became aware that
it was an act of arson,

00:00:56.856 --> 00:01:00.260
a hate crime, I chose to offer the keys

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:03.311
to our synagogue to the Muslim community.

00:01:03.311 --> 00:01:07.474
That was done without any
thought of religion or politics.

00:01:07.474 --> 00:01:10.827
About a decade ago, our
synagogue was desecrated

00:01:10.827 --> 00:01:13.333
with swastikas and "Heil, Hitler,"

00:01:13.333 --> 00:01:16.166
so we've been through this before.

00:01:17.265 --> 00:01:20.431
- There are a hundred
churches in Victoria, Texas,

00:01:20.431 --> 00:01:24.431
and then there's one mosque
and there's one synagogue.

00:01:24.431 --> 00:01:27.561
It's easy to fall in your
own little world and bubble.

00:01:27.561 --> 00:01:29.055
And yet, I would have never guessed

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:32.342
that the community would
have responded like this.

00:01:32.342 --> 00:01:35.184
I canceled Sunday school,
and I drove over there.

00:01:35.184 --> 00:01:39.109
I wanted to show my support
and solidarity for them.

00:01:39.109 --> 00:01:40.960
And I was thrilled to
see hundreds of people

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:42.475
come out of the woodwork and show up

00:01:42.475 --> 00:01:44.352
for these prayer services.

00:01:44.352 --> 00:01:45.504
- [Gary] We had Christians, Jews,

00:01:45.504 --> 00:01:47.477
Blacks, Whites, gays, straights

00:01:47.477 --> 00:01:50.688
together in solidarity with each other.

00:01:50.688 --> 00:01:53.557
When the attempts are made to divide us,

00:01:53.557 --> 00:01:55.627
actually, it backfires on the perpetrator

00:01:55.627 --> 00:01:57.176
'cause it really bands us all together

00:01:57.176 --> 00:01:58.843
as a cohesive group.

00:02:00.663 --> 00:02:02.743
- I remember standing, praying together

00:02:02.743 --> 00:02:06.604
with hundreds of community
members in front of us.

00:02:06.604 --> 00:02:09.751
The charred mosque was right behind us.

00:02:09.751 --> 00:02:14.316
And we almost turned our back
to the past, to the hate.

00:02:14.316 --> 00:02:16.647
And you feel there is
hope, not only for now

00:02:16.647 --> 00:02:18.230
but for the future.

00:02:19.709 --> 00:02:23.876
The outpouring of support was
a powerful message of healing.

00:02:24.792 --> 00:02:27.309
This came from a family in Oregon.

00:02:27.309 --> 00:02:29.848
"You are our brothers and sisters.

00:02:29.848 --> 00:02:34.015
"Never forget that there is
more love than you can see."

